Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Recover timestamp-rejected focus while the WM still selects us

A background client can advance the X server's last-focus-change timestamp
between a WM_TAKE_FOCUS offer and our response, including while waiting for
pointer grabs. XSetInputFocus then silently ignores the stale request.

If the request failed and _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW still selects the requested
window, get a fresh server timestamp through an unmapped InputOnly window
and retry once. Check the WM selection again after obtaining the timestamp.
A later focus change still supersedes the retry through normal X11 timestamp
ordering. No application or window-manager names are used.

Observed with Steam's deferred widget focus when AoE2 replaces its splash
window; the regression also reproduces using an isolated X server and the
actual set_focus function with its pointer wait stubbed.

Base: ValveSoftware/wine 7b3ceaf8644bb5d57140903e12897efac69be16a

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -671,6 +671,35 @@
 
 }
 
+/* XSetInputFocus silently ignores stale timestamps. A background client's
+ * focus restoration (Steam does this when a splash is destroyed) can advance
+ * the server's focus time while we wait for pointer grabs or process events.
+ * Retry once using a fresh server timestamp, but only while the WM still
+ * selects our window. Preserve timestamp ordering if the user switches away. */
+static void retry_rejected_focus( Display *display, Window window, Time time )
+{
+    XSetWindowAttributes attrs = {.event_mask = PropertyChangeMask};
+    Window focused, timestamp_window;
+    XEvent event;
+    int revert;
+
+    if (!time || !is_net_supported( x11drv_atom(_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW) )) return;
+    XGetInputFocus( display, &focused, &revert );
+    if (focused == window || get_net_active_window( display ) != window) return;
+
+    timestamp_window = XCreateWindow( display, DefaultRootWindow(display), 0, 0, 1, 1, 0,
+                                     0, InputOnly, CopyFromParent, CWEventMask, &attrs );
+    XChangeProperty( display, timestamp_window, x11drv_atom(TIMESTAMP), XA_INTEGER,
+                     8, PropModeAppend, NULL, 0 );
+    XWindowEvent( display, timestamp_window, PropertyChangeMask, &event );
+    XDestroyWindow( display, timestamp_window );
+
+    if (get_net_active_window( display ) != window) return;
+    TRACE( "retrying focus for window %lx with server time %lu (was %lu)\n",
+           window, event.xproperty.time, time );
+    XSetInputFocus( display, window, RevertToParent, event.xproperty.time );
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *              set_focus
  */
@@ -698,6 +727,7 @@
     {
         TRACE( "setting focus to %p (%lx) time=%ld\n", focus, win, time );
         XSetInputFocus( display, win, RevertToParent, time );
+        retry_rejected_focus( display, win, time );
     }
 }
 
